                373,
                1278
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In blast design, the number of situations where unsymmetrical bending occurs is limited and where encountered, it can be treated without serious economic penalty. Due to the fact that blast overpressure loads act normal to the surfaces of a structure, the use of doubly-symmetric cross sections for purlins and girts (e.g., hot-rolled S- and W-sections or cold-formed channels used back-to-back) is generally recommended. In such cases,the deformation criteria for flexural members in Section 5-22 apply.",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                1301,
                1041,
                1458
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
